WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:15.880
このようなことが起こらないことを願っていますが、麦わらの一味の誰かが死ぬ可能性はあるのでしょうか？

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:36.219
Hi, I asked the best one piece YouTube in
Japan the 17 most burning questions around

00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:37.219
the series.

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:41.280
2 weeks ago, I decided to share one of the
best one piece theories I have ever come across.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.280
This theory by Yuderon talked about the true
nature of laugh tale, the one piece as well

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.280
as the ancient kingdom.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.440
And after translating the video, condensing
it and adding my own thoughts and findings

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:52.190
on top, I published the video, gave it a very
daring title and went to bed with a feeling

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.129
that this might be interesting to those who
watched it.

00:00:56.129 --> 00:00:59.769
What I woke up to the next morning, was basically
chaos.

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:04.390
I was drowned in mentions and messages and
fighting my way to my channel page, I saw

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.660
that the video had gone viral.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.970
As of now said video stands at a staggering
two and a half million views.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:16.610
And I'm honestly still trying to process what
happened.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:22.280
Of course the real star here was Yuderon,
who's hard work and dedication to the story

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.280
made this all possible.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.980
And since many of you guys haven't had any
interactions with the Japanese anime and manga

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:26.980
community yet, I decided to ask Yuderon whether
he would be willing to do a little Q&amp;A, so

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:27.980
you could get to know him a bit better.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:28.980
So I gathered all your questions I received
on YouTube and Twitter and to not overwhelm

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:29.980
the poor man, condensed it into 17 ultimate
questions that I think cover the most ground

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:31.620
for what everyone wanted to know.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:36.880
Yuderon does weekly chapter previews, reviews
and theories on his channel and recently has

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.590
successfully predicted that Yamato would be
a righteous and female character.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:43.400
That Onigashima would be moved.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:48.070
That Yamato's mythical dog would play a role
in the story as well as the exact chapter

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:52.190
in which Jinbe officially joined with Luffy
and Co.

00:01:52.190 --> 00:02:03.230
Oh, and since we made this Q&amp;A in text-form
on Twitter, I asked one of my Japanese friends

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:08.720
to read Yuderon's replies, so it's a bit more
engaging.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.810
Thanks Shota!

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.440
Here we go.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.980
1.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.530
好きなキャラクターはいますか？その理由は？

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.960
I wouldn't have guessed that, but I definitely
know where he's coming from.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:24.960
Next.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:25.960
2.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:26.960
ONE PIECEに興味を持ったきっかけは何ですか？

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:27.960
Nice.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:28.960
Next.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:29.960
3.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:30.960
どのようにしてあなたのワンピース論を作っていますか？

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:31.960
Okay wow, this was a lot to digest.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:32.960
Yuderon has found 3 things Oda does regularly
that he bases his theories on.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.170
The mirrored structure of the story, that
we kind of know about in the west as well,

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:42.480
the wordplays and symbolism, which I'm personally
a big fan of.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.040
No wonder his theories are awesome.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.040
Next.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.040
4.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.040
日本では誰もが「ワンピース」を知っていると思われがちですが、日本における「ワンピース」の一般的なイメージはどのようなものなのでしょうか。なぜこんなに人気があるのでしょうか？

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.770
A lot of people asked this question, but I
think living here, I definitely agree with

00:02:51.770 --> 00:03:26.790
Yuderon, that people love One Piece and other
stories here for the same reasons as we do.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:04:26.660
Storytelling unites us all.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:41.620
Next.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:56.590
5.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:05:11.560
海外ではそれぞれのワンピース論や…日本では、ワンピースの話になるとどのような話題でしょうか？

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:15.080
Now I could blame this on my bad translation
of the question, but I'm gonna be a dick and

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.129
blame it on the question.

00:05:17.129 --> 00:05:36.039
See, there is no beef between Zoro and Sanji
in Japan.

00:05:36.039 --> 00:05:37.039
Next.

00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:38.039
6.

00:05:38.039 --> 00:05:39.039
あなたのワンピース論には日本語を知っているからこそ理解できるニュアンスがたくさん含まれます…翻訳で失われると感じるものは他にもありますか？

00:05:39.039 --> 00:05:42.120
I guess there wasn't really anything else
he could think of in terms of language barrier.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:46.659
From my personal experience though, I think
there are many references and other puns with

00:05:46.659 --> 00:05:50.860
names and so on, that make a lot more sense
as a Japanese person.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:57.789
Though I guess this is more a cultural and
less a language problem.

00:05:57.789 --> 00:06:02.249
Next.

00:06:02.249 --> 00:06:06.710
7.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:13.110
次はだれに麦わら帽子がわたるのかというのも是非聞いておきたいです
Okay this one was clearly my fuck up.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:17.879
I wanted to ask who he thinks the next straw
hat will be, but I butchered the translation.

00:06:17.879 --> 00:06:21.139
Luckily enough he gave me his answer later
on.

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:25.800
He also basis this on the wordplays with the
devil fruits, you might have come across before.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:31.520
Gomugomu, hitohito, hanahana, yomiyomi, leaving
2 and 9.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:41.289
By the way, when you add up these numbers:
56 + 110 + 87 + 43 + 29 you get 325, or san

00:06:41.289 --> 00:06:42.469
ni go.

00:06:42.469 --> 00:06:46.900
So for possible devil fruits, Yuderon gave
me the Nikyunikyu fruit, which is Kumas.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:53.319
The Fuku fuku fruit, which is Kinemons, the
jikijiki fruit, which is kids or the jukujuku

00:06:53.319 --> 00:06:55.330
fruit, which is SHinobus.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:07:01.360
Since Yamato would be inu, so 1 - 2, he thinks
she doesn't fit.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:06.550
He told me that he isn't really sure how it's
gonna play out, but he could imagine Franky

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:12.490
inheriting Kumas fruit and Vivi joining as
the 10th member, as that would connect past

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:13.569
and present again.

00:07:13.569 --> 00:07:17.439
First vivi wanted to join the crew anyways
and in one of the one piece magazines, the

00:07:17.439 --> 00:07:24.180
initial concept for the 10th member was titled
as Bolero, which would fit Vivi's image as

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:25.259
a dancer.

00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:40.069
I don't like that this makes sense, because
I still want Yamato to join.

00:07:40.069 --> 00:07:44.229
SO, next!

00:07:44.229 --> 00:07:46.309
8.

00:07:46.309 --> 00:07:48.399
誰もが憧れる尾田先生にお会いできるとしたら何を聞きたいですか？

00:07:48.399 --> 00:07:49.929
That's a very humble answer.

00:07:49.929 --> 00:08:01.169
I would probably ask Oda something important,
like why Sanji is so much stronger than Zoro.

00:08:01.169 --> 00:08:04.090
Next.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.020
9.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.949
海外のワンピース・コミュニティについて、どのようにお考えですか？

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:11.379
I'll leave that one to you guys.

00:08:11.379 --> 00:08:30.860
Let Yuderon and me know in the comments what

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:36.240
you think.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:41.620
Next!

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:47.000
10.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:52.380
尾田先生の大変な仕事ぶりは誰もが知っています。あなたの説では、マンガ家としての彼はほとんど人間離れしているように見えます。しかし、日本全体での一般的な尾田先生のイメージや仕事ぶりはどうなのでしょうか？

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.519
Man this one really shocked me.

00:08:54.519 --> 00:09:05.490
I think we should all stop complaining about
any breaks that Oda takes.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:42.380
The poor man 

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:54.889
deserves some rest.

00:09:54.889 --> 00:10:00.889
Next.

00:10:00.889 --> 00:10:06.889
12.

00:10:06.889 --> 00:10:12.889
語呂合わせというと、欧米のファンは小田先生の使う語呂合わせには懐疑的な人が多いですね。ユデロンさんの作品にはそのような語呂合わせの話が多く見られます。これは尾田さんが本当にわざとやっているのではないかと思うのですが、いかがですか？

00:10:12.889 --> 00:10:31.459
This was so interesting to 

00:10:31.459 --> 00:10:32.459
me to hear.

00:10:32.459 --> 00:10:39.310
I originally was REALLY no fan of these wordplay
things, but I've completely changed my mind.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:11:01.329
Let#s wait for chapter 1031 I guess and see

00:11:01.329 --> 00:11:02.329
what happens.

00:11:02.329 --> 00:11:03.329
Next!

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:04.329
13.

00:11:04.329 --> 00:11:05.329
和の国は今、クライマックスを迎えています。しかし、和の国の次はどのような冒険になるのとお考えでしょうか？

00:11:05.329 --> 00:11:15.029
I really can't tell you how ready I am for
ELbaf and finding out what happened at 

00:11:15.029 --> 00:11:16.029
the reverie!

00:11:16.029 --> 00:11:17.029
Next!

00:11:17.029 --> 00:11:18.029
14.

00:11:18.029 --> 00:11:19.029
月が『ワンピース』の象徴としていかに重要であるかは、広く知られています。エネルは月に行ったこともあります。実際の月は物語の中で重要な役割を果たすと思いますか？

00:11:19.029 --> 00:11:51.050
Never thought of this, but it makes so much
sense my head hurts.

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:59.810
That would truly be an ancient weapon.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:06.630
Next!

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:13.439
15.

00:12:13.439 --> 00:12:20.259
時折、「ワンピースはもうすぐ終わる」と言われていますが、まだまだ終わりには程遠い感じがします。ユデロンさんは、ワンピースの最終章が見られるのはいつになると思いますか？

00:12:20.259 --> 00:12:22.939
I kind of feel the same way if I'm being honest.

00:12:22.939 --> 00:12:28.500
I want the story to continue on forever, but
also want to see how it ends.

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:29.710
Ahh, the dilemma.

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:30.710
Next.

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:31.710
16.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:32.710
古代兵器についてはどうお考えですか？彼らの目的は何ですか？

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:54.920
I 

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:55.920
like that idea.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:00.189
I've also thought about it along the lines
that the ancient weapons really depend on

00:13:00.189 --> 00:13:01.480
who uses them and how.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:07.410
They might truly be just really great pieces
of technology or powers that pose a threat

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:13.920
to the world government.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:17.079
Next.

00:13:17.079 --> 00:13:20.240
17.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:23.399
日本語を話せない多くの人々が、あなたのビデオを見たいと思っています。動画を英語に翻訳する予定はありますか？

00:13:23.399 --> 00:13:27.860
There you have it guys, make sure to subscribe
to Yuderon, his channel is linked in the description.

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:28.860
Next.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:43.019
Here's a bonus for sticking around till 
the end.

